    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ z_{oi} $ and $ z_{pi} $ represent the offspring and parent phenotypes for the ith family, $ \\alpha = \\mu_o - \\beta_{op} \\mu_p $ is the intercept, $ \\beta_{op} $ is the regression coefficient, and $ e_i $ is the residual deviation from the regression. In statistical terms, from Chapter 3 we know that the least-squares regression coefficient, $ b_{op} = \\text{Cov}(z_o, z_p) / \\text{Var}(z_p) $, provides an estimate of $ \\beta_{op} $. If there are no environmental causes of resemblance between parents and offspring, we then have (from Chapter 7),",
      "source_page": 552,
      "printed_page": 532,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter17:p002:b7"
      ],
      "bbox": [
