    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Thus, under the stated assumptions, a simple (possibly upwardly biased) estimate of $ h^{2} = \\sigma_{A}^{2} / \\sigma_{z}^{2} $ is twice the (single) parent-offspring regression, $ 2b_{op} $.",
