    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Greater precision is possible when both parents can be measured, as one can then regress offspring phenotypes on the mean phenotypes of their parents (also known as the midparent values). Our model is now slightly altered to become",
      "source_page": 552,
      "printed_page": 532,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter17:p002:b11"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        112.0,
