    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ z_{mi} $ and $ z_{fi} $ refer to the phenotypes of mothers and fathers. The least-squares slope of the midparent-offspring regression, $ b_{o\\overline{p}} $, is a direct estimate of the heritability. To obtain this result, let us assume that the phenotypic variance is the same in both sexes and in both generations and that the resemblance between relatives is independent of their sex. We then have",
      "source_page": 552,
      "printed_page": 532,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter17:p002:b13"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        112.0,
